IESNA:LM-63-2002
[TEST]      synthetic non-axisymmetric fixture for h-frame convention test
[MANUFAC]   none
[LUMCAT]    SIN-H-FULL
[LAMP]      idealised
[ISSUEDATE] 2026-05-11
[OTHER]     Used by tests/iesHframeOrientation to verify that the
[OTHER]     iesEmitter BC's world-direction-to-(gamma, h) conversion
[OTHER]     and iesPhotometry's table lookup share a consistent sign
[OTHER]     convention for h on a non-axisymmetric IES file.
[OTHER]
[OTHER]     Symmetry: FULL (last horizontal angle = 315 != 90 / 180),
[OTHER]     so the table is treated as cyclic without folding. The
[OTHER]     four 90 deg-spaced stored h values map to four distinct
[OTHER]     world directions in the BC's perpendicular frame.
[OTHER]
[OTHER]     gamma values: 0, 30, 60, 90 (flat across this range; no
[OTHER]                  back emission so gamma > 90 is omitted).
[OTHER]     h values:     0, 45, 90, 135, 180, 225, 270, 315 deg
[OTHER]     intensity:    F(h) = 5 + 4 sin(h), independent of gamma.
[OTHER]                   Peak at h = 90 (F = 9), trough at h = 270
[OTHER]                   (F = 1), equal at h = 0 and h = 180 (F = 5).
[OTHER]                   Symmetric about the (h=0, h=180) axis.
[OTHER]                   The +-90 antipodal asymmetry distinguishes
[OTHER]                   the CCW vs CW handedness of the BC's
[OTHER]                   atan2(dPerp . e2, dPerp . fixtureUp).
